+no one out, since every server holds the same key.
+
+## Logging out one member
+
+`logout(member_id)` in `larder/sessions.py` ends a member's current session right away, for a volunteer handling a
+lost or stolen phone. It is kept in memory on the server that handles the call, not in the cookie, so it is lost on
+restart and, if larder is running on more than one web server, only logs the member out of the one that saw the
+call - rotate `LARDER_SESSION_KEY` instead to be certain, at the cost of logging everyone out. A member who logs in
+again after being logged out gets a new, valid session.
 
